      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case is reported of a 180 degrees levorotation of the gravid uterus with successful outcome for mother and child. Delivery was by cesarean section.Only 108 cases of rotation of the gravid uterus have been reported in the world's literature. A uterine tumour was associated in almost one third of cases. The condition usually presents as an acute abdomen. Complications include uterine rupture and pulmonary embolism. Treatment is by laparotomy and de-torsion, with cesarean section if at term or near term."},
